{"t": 1787385339.049, "op": "update", "id": 2, "chars": 1463, "content": "sphinx-rfm clone: on OLD checkout states (3.0.x aca3f825f; 4.x-era 232dbe41c, Oct 2021) app-based tests and real builds fail at startup (ExtensionError/VersionRequirementError) because the venv's sphinxcontrib.applehelp/devhelp/htmlhelp/serializinghtml/qthelp and alabaster are too new \u2014 sphinx/application.py unconditionally loads them as builtin extensions. Workaround there: prepend a stubs dir to PYTHONPATH containing a regular `sphinxcontrib` package with stub modules whose `setup(app)` returns {\"version\": \"stub\", \"parallel_read_safe\": True}, plus an `alabaster` stub package that appends the real site-packages alabaster dir to its `__path__` (theme.conf needs `alabaster.support`) and provides `get_path()`; usage `PYTHONPATH=<stubs> python -m pytest ...` (stubs lived in /tmp/sphinx_type_hint_links/stubs; /tmp gets cleared, recreate if needed). HOWEVER at the 5.2.0-dev state (f35d2a6cc, Sep 2022) NO stubs are needed: `python -m pytest tests/...` and `python -m sphinx -b html ...` work directly (~650 tests pass; only tests/test_build_html.py::test_html_code_role and tests/test_build_latex.py::test_latex_code_role fail pre-existing, Pygments version). Check `git log -1` first to see which era the checkout is in. flake8/mypy are not installed in the venv (use awk on line length; setup.cfg max-line-length = 95). For manual builds use `html_theme = 'basic'`; intersphinx accepts a local `objects.inv` path (hand-craft v2 format) to avoid network.", "accesses": 24, "value": 0.5352021084580383, "outcomes": 20}
